<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 17th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1600s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/17th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1650 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10232 5385" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1650 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="7018" cy="1385" r="174"/><text x="7018" y="1458" font-size="209">1</text></g><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="174"/><text x="5709" y="1043" font-size="209">2</text></g><g><circle cx="4997" cy="651" r="174"/><text x="4997" y="724" font-size="209">3</text></g><g><circle cx="2883" cy="2883" r="174"/><text x="2883" y="2956" font-size="209">4</text></g><g><circle cx="7752" cy="1900" r="174"/><text x="7752" y="1973" font-size="209">5</text></g><g><circle cx="7567" cy="1068" r="174"/><text x="7567" y="1141" font-size="209">6</text></g><g><circle cx="8530" cy="1145" r="174"/><text x="8530" y="1218" font-size="209">7</text></g><g><circle cx="6029" cy="1964" r="174"/><text x="6029" y="2037" font-size="209">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1650 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Tokugawa Shogunate &middot; Ottoman Empire &middot; Qing Empire &middot; Viceroyalty of Peru &middot; Ayutthaya Kingdom &middot; British Empire &middot; Ethiopian Empire &middot; Mughal Empire</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaties of Nijmegen</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Sekigahara</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Thirty Years' War</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaty of the Pyrenees</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Peace of Westphalia</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Glorious Revolution</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Louis XIV</li><li>Shivaji</li><li>Johannes Kepler</li><li>Oliver Cromwell</li><li>Albrecht von Wallenstein</li><li>Charles X Gustav</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1630–1680</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1583–1634</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1571–1630</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1622–1660</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1599–1658</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1638–1715</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Guerrilla warfare</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Hill fort</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1600s, 386 recorded states were founded and 215 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Mughal Empire, the Ottoman Empire and the British Empire. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 17th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/17th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 17th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Mughal Empire <span>1526 CE – 1857 CE</span></li><li>Ottoman Empire <span>1299 CE – 1922 CE</span></li><li>British Empire <span>1583 CE – 1997 CE</span></li><li>Viceroyalty of Peru <span>1542 CE – 1824 CE</span></li><li>Ayutthaya Kingdom <span>1351 CE – 1767 CE</span></li><li>Qing Empire <span>1644 CE – 1912 CE</span></li><li>Tokugawa Shogunate <span>1603 CE – 1868 CE</span></li><li>Ethiopian Empire <span>1270 CE – 1974 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Battle of Sekigahara <span>1600</span></li><li>Thirty Years' War <span>1618–1648</span></li><li>Peace of Westphalia <span>1648</span></li><li>Treaty of the Pyrenees <span>7 November 1659</span></li><li>Treaties of Nijmegen <span>1678–1679</span></li><li>Glorious Revolution <span>1688–1689</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Louis XIV <span>6: 1638–1715</span></li><li>Shivaji <span>1: 1630–1680</span></li><li>Johannes Kepler <span>3: 1571–1630</span></li><li>Oliver Cromwell <span>5: 1599–1658</span></li><li>Albrecht von Wallenstein <span>2: 1583–1634</span></li><li>Charles X Gustav <span>4: 1622–1660</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Guerrilla warfare</dt><dd>Guerrilla warfare is a form of irregular warfare in which small, mobile forces use raids, ambushes and knowledge of terrain against larger conventional armies.</dd><dt>Hill fort</dt><dd>A hill fort is a fortification built on high ground, using the natural terrain for defence.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
